<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1874&lastnode_id=175">Fear II</a> (3 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=207&lastnode_id=175">Voness</a> on 2001-06-07 15:04:08</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2> Greetings Bloodhorde,<br>
  Well, we went to Fear, and got our noses bloodied abit. We all know what the flaw was in my insertions plan ( I had no idea that crashing the Gate would literally carsh the zone). So, I am looking forward to trying again. I think we will stay away from weeknight raids from this point on. Our varied schedules caused a bit of a problem in group balancing. With that in mind, I'd like to try again Saturday at 1pm PST. I had thought that I'd be working on Saturday, and that is why I planned for this previous Wed. night. But, I was informed today that I will only need to work 1/2 a day on Saturday ( I guess my efficiancy at work is a bit better than it is on Fear break-ins =/ ) Anyway, I know that we lost alot of XP Wed. night, some of us died 3 or 4 times, but I think we need to go back while we are still a little bent about this, and show the minions of Cazic Thule who's who around here. Everyone that bought coffins with money from their own accounts, either send me a tell in game, or E-Mail me (  dcfans@nvbell.net  ) and I'll get that money back to you.  <br>
<br>
Voness Dyr'Fate<br>
Circle of Bones<br>
Raid Saboteur<br>
Bloodhorde</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1869&lastnode_id=175">Well, it's official...</a> (13 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=983&lastnode_id=175">Gnormagn</a> on 2001-06-07 13:21:23</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Verant is not going to help me recover my account.  I received this email today from Phillip Wiglesworth, a.k.a. Nangwaya.<br>
<br>
"Greetings,<br>
<br>
Although I fully understand and sympathize with the circumstances that<br>
caused experience loss to your characters and loss of items, I cannot<br>
restore or reimburse items and/or experience lost due to your account being<br>
compromised by a third party.  The security of a customer's account is the<br>
responsibility of the owner, something we cannot have any control over.  I<br>
apoligize if you feel you have been misled in this situation.  I had<br>
originally assumed the Guide Staff had relayed this information to you, and<br>
I also apoligize that this did not happen.  If you have any further<br>
questions, please feel free to respond to this email.<br>
<br>
Sincerely,<br>
Game Master Nangwaya, Terris-Thule<br>
Sony Online Entertainment<br>
pwiglesworth@station.sony.com<br>
http://www.station.sony.com"<br>
<br>
I'm beside myself.  I have no idea what to do now.  What I thought was just bad customer service and apathy turns out to be a policy that I cannot do anything about.  I could reply to him... but what will that accomplish?  I feel cheated and violated, and there's nothing I can do.<br>
<br>
As of this posting, I'm retiring from EQ.  I invested over 50 days of play time into Gnorm, just to have it all raped away by some hacker, and the GMs are saying they can do nothing to help.<br>
<br>
It was great being able to hunt with all of you for all of this time, both as Nulliira back on Karana and Gnormagn on Terris-Thule.  I'll be living the EQ experience vicariously through Gnadira, Razorr and Frostooth, who I'm sure will be telling me all of thier exploits.<br>
<br>
When a new game comes out, one that I have some faith in, I'll hopefully be able to join up with some of you again.<br>
<br>
- John</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
