<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1809&lastnode_id=175">Account Debacles, Redux</a> (8 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=983&lastnode_id=175">Gnormagn</a> on 2001-05-29 08:41:26</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>This is all OOC, and I'm sorry to take Voness' spot as the top story...<br>
<br>
My account's been hacked, again.  This time they not only changed my password, but my Station info was changed so I couldn't even get my password mailed to me.  I went through every automated facet of the EQ website with no luck.<br>
<br>
A phone call to Verant this morning fixed me up, but my accoutn is f'ed.  Gnorm is down to level 45 from 48.  All of my equipment is gone.  My bank is wiped out.  A new Erudite character that I did not create is in my account.  I'm KOS in Neriak, too... and I'm bound there.  Should be fun to try and fix this.<br>
<br>
I'm petitioning now to get this fixed.. but...<br>
<br>
If any of you saw me this weekend, IT WAS NOT ME.  I was not online since Thursday night.  If you hear stories of rotten things I've done this weekend, it wasn't me.  I swear this to you.<br>
<br>
My account's clearly been compromised in a very bad way.  I'm going to make attempts to change my station name.  I don't know what else to do...<br>
<br>
See you all, I hope, soon.<br>
<br>
- J, aka Gnormagn Fudder</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1802&lastnode_id=175">Bloodhorde invades Hate.......    News at 11</a> (3 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=207&lastnode_id=175">Voness</a> on 2001-05-25 15:50:26</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Greetings Bloodhorde,<br>
  After many weeks of planning and scheming, I have put together an invasion plan that meets the Warlord's standards. The Bloodhorde will show Innoruuk and the rest of Norrath who is the most evil, corrupt and destructive force around. <br>
<br>
(ooc) Saturday, June 2nd at 9am PST (12 Noon EST) is the time. South Ro Wizard Pyramid is the place. All Bloodhorde Members 2 orange bubbles into 46 or better are invited. I ask that everyone bring any Poison, Disease and Magic resistance items you have, or can get between now and then. I will go over insertion plans and loot rules before lift off on Saturday. I will be inviting a few outside members for services they can offer and to loot up some of the items we cannot use (ie Paladin gear, Ranger gear and such). It is very important that we have a large turnout for this event. The less people that show up, the less our chances are of going. Some key members will be Kloth, Kolu, Kajen, and Xedoc. All for obvious reasons. I am already making plans for our first Dragon hunt, and will continue making those plans if the turnout here is good. I plan to take most of the lower floor. If we have a good turnout, and fight well, we will attempt to kill the Maestro and his hand, and possibly one or more of the mini bosses on the second floor (depending on spawn).<br>
<br>
Also I will be giving instructions during the raid. If you have been to Hate before, and feel like you don't need much instruction, that is fine. But, please humor me while we are there. The idea here is to get some raid experience and loots for those members that have yet to take part in such events. Those of us who have been there and done that need to lead by example so as to make this an enjoyable experience for all. If you have been there and done that, I'm sure you know what kind of stress and disappointment a bad raid can bring.<br>
<br>
I won't ask you to post if you WILL be there, but rather post if you CANNOT make it. I'm sure that list will be shorter.<br>
<br>
(ic) Now, go....  go collect your weapons and wits. You will need them both come the day of our advance. Good day, and see you there. (/salute)<br>
<br>
Voness Dyr'Fate<br>
Circle of Bones<br>
</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>
